13
00:00:53,668 --> 00:00:57,620
because we were measuring wind direction, and we'd brought the compass for that...

14
00:00:57,620 --> 00:01:01,840
But not the piece of string to hold up in the air!

15
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:06,060
Didn't Mr Blake make a fuss about us leaving that behind? Yeah.

16
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:10,720
He does go on. Anyway it was easy to get one from another of the students.

17
00:01:10,720 --> 00:01:16,840
Now, the next sections the procedure. I sent you the draft of that. Yeah.

18
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:23,041
It was clear, but I don't think we need all these details of what time we left

19
00:01:23,041 --> 00:01:28,020
